From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the bundled cxxopts licence

The extension statically compiles in `tools/ibzip2.cpp` (for the
bundled `ibzip2` CLI entry point), which `#include <cxxopts.hpp>` from
the `src/external/cxxopts` submodule (MIT, Jarryd Beck). The explicit
`license-files` list only names this package's own two licences, so
it does not fall back to setuptools' `LICEN[CS]E*` auto-discovery
glob and cxxopts' licence is silently dropped from the wheel despite
being compiled in. Confirmed on the real published PyPI wheel
(indexed_bzip2-1.7.0-cp312-*): dist-info carries only LICENSE-APACHE
and LICENSE-MIT.

`src` is a symlink to the repository's top-level `src/`, so the added
glob entry resolves through it to the submodule's own LICENSE file
with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against mxmlnkn/indexed_bzip2]
---
 python/indexed_bzip2/pyproject.toml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/python/indexed_bzip2/pyproject.toml b/python/indexed_bzip2/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/python/indexed_bzip2/pyproject.toml
+++ b/python/indexed_bzip2/pyproject.toml
@@ -67,4 +67,5 @@
 license-files = [
     "LICENSE-APACHE",
     "LICENSE-MIT",
+    "src/external/cxxopts/LICENSE",
 ]
--
2.43.0
